    {
      "id": "ssmh2kj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Characteristics of Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plant cells contain cell walls made of cellulose, chloroplasts for light absorption, and large central vacuoles.",
        "Plant tissues are categorized into Meristematic (active cell division) and Permanent (specialized functional) tissues.",
        "Photosynthesis takes place in chloroplasts, converting light energy into chemical energy to synthesize glucose.",
        "Plant reproduction occurs through both sexual mechanisms via flowers and asexual methods via vegetative propagation.",
        "Phytohormones including Auxins, Gibberellins, Cytokinins, Abscisic Acid, and Ethylene regulate growth and responses."
      ],
      "id": "9y347y2"
    },
